    "q-223742": {
      "dom_id": "step-q223742",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "In **ascending order**, the solutions to $\\frac{1}{5}{t}^{2}=-3t$ are $t=${{field-1}} and $t=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we move all of the terms to the left-hand side and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{t}^{2} & =-3t \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}{t}^{2}+3t & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}t(t+15) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the zero product rule to get\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}t=0\\,\\text{or}\\,t+15=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\nt=0\\,\\text{or}\\,t=-15.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $t=-15$ and $t=0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
